{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780287264418,"sessionID":"ses_17e9c69d9ffejSPYsh82mlETBG","part":{"id":"prt_e8163d561001e6UmMT7fc8euZM","sessionID":"ses_17e9c69d9ffejSPYsh82mlETBG","messageID":"msg_e8163c802001K3SkVyjJJDWEn0","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_k45x8v3g0tbh_1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/02-components/font.md","limit":120},"output":"<file>\n00001| ---\n00002| title: Font Module\n00003| nav_title: Font\n00004| description: Optimizing loading web fonts with the built-in `next/font` loaders.\n00005| ---\n00006| \n00007| {/* The content of this doc is shared between the app and pages router. You can use the `<PagesOnly>Content</PagesOnly>` component to add content that is specific to the Pages Router. Any shared content should not be wrapped in a component. */}\n00008| \n00009| [`next/font`](/docs/app/api-reference/components/font) automatically optimizes your fonts (including custom fonts) and removes external network requests for improved privacy and performance.\n00010| \n00011| It includes **built-in automatic self-hosting** for any font file. This means you can optimally load web fonts with no [layout shift](https://web.dev/articles/cls).\n00012| \n00013| You can also conveniently use all [Google Fonts](https://fonts.google.com/). CSS and font files are downloaded at build time and self-hosted with the rest of your static assets. **No requests are sent to Google by the browser.**\n00014| \n00015| <AppOnly>\n00016| \n00017| ```tsx filename=\"app/layout.tsx\" switcher\n00018| import { Inter } from 'next/font/google'\n00019| \n00020| // If loading a variable font, you don't need to specify the font weight\n00021| const inter = Inter({\n00022|   subsets: ['latin'],\n00023|   display: 'swap',\n00024| })\n00025| \n00026| export default function RootLayout({\n00027|   children,\n00028| }: {\n00029|   children: React.ReactNode\n00030| }) {\n00031|   return (\n00032|     <html lang=\"en\" className={inter.className}>\n00033|       <body>{children}</body>\n00034|     </html>\n00035|   )\n00036| }\n00037| ```\n00038| \n00039| ```jsx filename=\"app/layout.js\" switcher\n00040| import { Inter } from 'next/font/google'\n00041| \n00042| // If loading a variable font, you don't need to specify the font weight\n00043| const inter = Inter({\n00044|   subsets: ['latin'],\n00045|   display: 'swap',\n00046| })\n00047| \n00048| export default function RootLayout({ children }) {\n00049|   return (\n00050|     <html lang=\"en\" className={inter.className}>\n00051|       <body>{children}</body>\n00052|     </html>\n00053|   )\n00054| }\n00055| ```\n00056| \n00057| </AppOnly>\n00058| \n00059| <PagesOnly>\n00060| \n00061| To use the font in all your pages, add it to [`_app.js` file](/docs/pages/building-your-application/routing/custom-app) under `/pages` as shown below:\n00062| \n00063| ```jsx filename=\"pages/_app.js\"\n00064| import { Inter } from 'next/font/google'\n00065| \n00066| // If loading a variable font, you don't need to specify the font weight\n00067| const inter = Inter({ subsets: ['latin'] })\n00068| \n00069| export default function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {\n00070|   return (\n00071|     <main className={inter.className}>\n00072|       <Component {...pageProps} />\n00073|     </main>\n00074|   )\n00075| }\n00076| ```\n00077| \n00078| </PagesOnly>\n00079| \n00080| > **🎥 Watch:** Learn more about using `next/font` → [YouTube (6 minutes)](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L8_98i_bMMA).\n00081| \n00082| ## Reference\n00083| \n00084| | Key                                         | `font/google`       | `font/local`        | Type                       | Required          |\n00085| | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------- |\n00086| | [`src`](#src)                               | <Cross size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | String or Array of Objects | Yes               |\n00087| | [`weight`](#weight)                         | <Check size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | String or Array            | Required/Optional |\n00088| | [`style`](#style)                           | <Check size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | String or Array            | -                 |\n00089| | [`subsets`](#subsets)                       | <Check size={18} /> | <Cross size={18} /> | Array of Strings           | -                 |\n00090| | [`axes`](#axes)                             | <Check size={18} /> | <Cross size={18} /> | Array of Strings           | -                 |\n00091| | [`display`](#display)                       | <Check size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | String                     | -                 |\n00092| | [`preload`](#preload)                       | <Check size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | Boolean                    | -                 |\n00093| | [`fallback`](#fallback)                     | <Check size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | Array of Strings           | -                 |\n00094| | [`adjustFontFallback`](#adjustfontfallback) | <Check size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | Boolean or String          | -                 |\n00095| | [`variable`](#variable)                     | <Check size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | String                     | -                 |\n00096| | [`declarations`](#declarations)             | <Cross size={18} /> | <Check size={18} /> | Array of Objects           | -                 |\n00097| \n00098| ### `src`\n00099| \n00100| The path of the font file as a string or an array of objects (with type `Array<{path: string, weight?: string, style?: string}>`) relative to the directory where the font loader function is called.\n00101| \n00102| Used in `next/font/local`\n00103| \n00104| - Required\n00105| \n00106| Examples:\n00107| \n00108| - `src:'./fonts/my-font.woff2'` where `my-font.woff2` is placed in a directory named `fonts` inside the `app` directory\n00109| - `src:[{path: './inter/Inter-Thin.ttf', weight: '100',},{path: './inter/Inter-Regular.ttf',weight: '400',},{path: './inter/Inter-Bold-Italic.ttf', weight: '700',style: 'italic',},]`\n00110| - if the font loader function is called in `app/page.tsx` using `src:'../styles/fonts/my-font.ttf'`, then `my-font.ttf` is placed in `styles/fonts` at the root of the project\n00111| \n00112| ### `weight`\n00113| \n00114| The font [`weight`](https://fonts.google.com/knowledge/glossary/weight) with the following possibilities:\n00115| \n00116| - A string with possible values of the weights available for the specific font or a range of values if it's a [variable](https://fonts.google.com/variablefonts) font\n00117| - An array of weight values if the font is not a [variable google font](https://fonts.google.com/variablefonts). It applies to `next/font/google` only.\n00118| \n00119| Used in `next/font/google` and `next/font/local`\n00120| \n\n(File has more lines. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 120)\n</file>","title":"node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/02-components/font.md","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Font Module\nnav_title: Font\ndescription: Optimizing loading web fonts with the built-in `next/font` loaders.\n---\n\n{/* The content of this doc is shared between the app and pages router. You can use the `<PagesOnly>Content</PagesOnly>` component to add content that is specific to the Pages Router. Any shared content should not be wrapped in a component. */}\n\n[`next/font`](/docs/app/api-reference/components/font) automatically optimizes your fonts (including custom fonts) and removes external network requests for improved privacy and performance.\n\nIt includes **built-in automatic self-hosting** for any font file. This means you can optimally load web fonts with no [layout shift](https://web.dev/articles/cls).\n\nYou can also conveniently use all [Google Fonts](https://fonts.google.com/). CSS and font files are downloaded at build time and self-hosted with the rest of your static assets. **No requests are sent to Google by the browser.**\n\n<AppOnly>\n\n```tsx filename=\"app/layout.tsx\" switcher\nimport { Inter } from 'next/font/google'\n\n// If loading a variable font, you don't need to specify the font weight"},"time":{"start":1780287264416,"end":1780287264417}}}}
